    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="28">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 28</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="330" ed="#liebermann"/>And þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> nan man nænne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_28.lnote.oe.8"/> man ne underfo na længc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_28.lnote.oe.9"/> þonne þreo niht, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_28.lnote.oe.10"/> hine se befæste, þe he ær folgade.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_28.lnote.oe.11"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="330" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> nan man nænne man underfó na leng ðonne III niht, buton híne se befæste, ðe he ær folgade.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="330" ed="#liebermann"/>And þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> nan man nenne man ne underfo na leng þonne þreo niht, buton he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_28.lnote.oe.2"/> hine befeaste se, ðe he ær folgade.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="331" ed="#liebermann"/>Et nemo suscipiat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_28.lnote.oe.4"/> aliquem ultra trinoctium, nisi ipse commendet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_28.lnote.oe.5"/>, cui antea seruiuit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="331" ed="#liebermann"/>Nemo teneat aliquem hominem diutius tribus noctibus, nisi dominus eius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_28.lnote.oe.3"/>, cui prius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_28.lnote.oe.4-2"/> seruiuit, eum commendauerit. Quodsi aliter fecerit, persoluat priori<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_28.lnote.oe.5-2"/> domino despectum eius et regi forisfacturam suam.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="331" ed="#liebermann"/>Nec quisquam suscipiat quemquam diucius quam tribus noctibus, nisi ipse illum commendet, cui olim seruierat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="28" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="188" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ þæt nan man nænne man underfó<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_28.robnote.fn.6"/> na leng ðonne III niht, buton híne se befæste ð<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_28.robnote.fn.7"/>e he ær folgade.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="268" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And þæt nan man nænne man ne underfo na længc þonne þreo niht, butan hine se befæste, þe he ær folgade.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="330" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_28.lnote.de.1"/> dass niemand einen Mann länger als drei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_28.lnote.de.2"/> Nächte aufnehme, wenn denselben nicht der empfiehlt, welchem derselbe bisher commendirt war.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_28.lnote.de.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And that no one receive any man for longer than three nights unless the one whom he previously served commends him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="189" ed="#robertson"/>And no-one shall entertain any man for more than three days, unless he is committed to his charge by the man whom he has been serving<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_28.robnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_28.whinote.n.4"/><pb n="465" ed="#whitelock"/>And no one is to entertain any man for more than three days, unless he whom he previously served commits him to him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="269" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And no one shall detain a servant for more than three nights unless the latter has been entrusted to him by the person he previously followed.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="330"><ref target="clause:IIAs_22">II As 22</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II As. 22</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_48">Leis Wl 48</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_22">II As 22</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 28-28:1: II As 22, 22:2</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_22-2">II As 22.2</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 28-28:1: II As 22, 22:2</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="465"><label>like in content</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_22">II As 22</ref> <quote>This and the following clause are like II Athelstan, 22, 22.2, in content, but not in wording.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="465"><label>like in content</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_22-2">II As 22.2</ref> <quote>This and the following clause are like II Athelstan, 22, 22.2, in content, but not in wording.</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">A's ‘he’ should perhaps be struck. Liebermann compares II As 22.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 331, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">ne: omitted B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">butan: butan he A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">331</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a. s. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a. s. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">331</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">emendet cui ante <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">emendet cui ante K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">330</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nenne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nenne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">330</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">leng <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">leng Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">330</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton se h. b. se þe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton se h. b. se þe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">330</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gode <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gode Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">330</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">besser zu streichen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">better deleted</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">331</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">331</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">plus <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">plus Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">331</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt durch Hn 8, 5, übersetzt durch Leis Wl 48</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used by Hn 8, 5, translated by Leis Wl 48</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Fremde 12</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Fremde 12</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_28.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zur Busse für Ungehorsam (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 26c) in Inst <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>. V As 1³·⁴. Das Strafgeld an den König für Aufnahme des anderswo entlaufenen Gefolges (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 8c. d, wo II Ew 7 zu zitieren war) ist Königs ‘Ungehorsam’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On the compensation for disobedience (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 26c) in Inst <hi rend="italic">cf</hi>. V As 1³·⁴. The fine to the king for receiving a retainer who has run away from elsewhere (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> Gefolge in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 8c. d, where II Ew 7 should have been cited) is the king's ‘disobedience’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_28.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. Hl. 15; II Edw. 7; II As. 22.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_28.robnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><label>underfó</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ne u.</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_28.robnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><label>ðe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">buton he</hi> (<hi rend="italic">se</hi>) <hi rend="italic">h. b. se ðe</hi> A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_28.whinote.n.4" n="4" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">465</biblScope></bibl><label>28</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">This and the following clause are like II Athelstan, 22, 22.2, in content, but not in wording.</seg></note>
      </div>
